 "title": "Picked Last, Beat a Giant: College Hoops' Wildest Week",
 "voice": "am_michael",
 "speed": 1.0,
 "description": "Two college basketball giants lost to schools almost nobody picked in the first week of the 2026-27 season. On Nov 2, 2026, East Texas A&M, picked 12th of 12 in the Southland preseason poll, beat Oklahoma 68-64 in Norman as a 28.5-point underdog: per ESPN Research, the second-largest Division I upset by point spread in 30 years (only Eastern Illinois over Iowa in 2022 was bigger). On Nov 6, Valparaiso beat Purdue 83-80 in double overtime at Mackey Arena on Justus McNair's buzzer-beating three, its first win over Purdue since 1965. We go through both games, the history, the money gap after the House v. NCAA settlement ($20.5M revenue-sharing cap per school in 2025-26), and the reasons small teams win: three-point shooting, free throws and turnovers, early-season timing, and simply playing well. Real people appear only as generic labelled stick figures; quotes are as reported by the sources below.\n\nWe don't pick sides. We just count the facts.\n\nSources:\nAP via News 9, Oklahoma stunned by East Texas A&M in 68-64 season-opening loss (Nov 2, 2026): https://www.news9.com/sports/university-of-oklahoma/oklahoma-stunned-by-east-texas-a-m-in-68-64-season-opening-loss\nClutchPoints, Porter Moser apologizes after loss to East Texas A&M (Nov 3, 2026): https://clutchpoints.com/ncaa-basketball/oklahoma-basketball-news-porter-moser-forced-apologize-loss-east-texas-am-28-5-point-favorite\nYardbarker, We already have our first stunning upset of the season (Nov 3, 2026): https://www.yardbarker.com/college_basketball/articles/we_already_have_our_first_stunning_upset_of_the_2026_27_college_basketball_season/s1_13132_44510412\nField Level Media via Yardbarker, Valparaiso shocks Purdue on buzzer-beater in 2nd OT (Nov 6, 2026): https://www.yardbarker.com/college_basketball/articles/valparaiso_shocks_purdue_on_buzzer_beater_in_2nd_ot/s1_17048_44526859\nNCAA.com, 21 years in the making: How a prayer led to Valparaiso's historic win over Purdue (Nov 7, 2026): https://www.ncaa.com/news/basketball-men/article/2026-11-07/21-years-making-how-prayer-led-valparaiso-mens-basketballs-historic-win-over\nPurdue Boilermakers On SI via Yahoo Sports, 5 takeaways from Purdue's stunning 83-80 loss to Valparaiso (Nov 7, 2026): https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/5-takeaways-purdues-stunning-83-023319783.html\nFront Office Sports, The year schools paid their players: https://frontofficesports.com/the-year-schools-paid-their-players/\n\n#collegebasketball #upset #underdog #marchmadness #ncaa #valparaiso #purdue #oklahoma #explained #stickfigure",
